# crescent UI needs no environment variables to run the registry or the
# showcase site. Everything below is OPTIONAL.

# Analytics (PostHog) — opt-in. Leave everything unset and nothing loads: no
# snippet is rendered, all capture() calls are no-ops, and the registry is still
# served (just without counting). All keys below can share one PostHog project.

# Client-side (showcase site): pageview/visitor tracking + the
# `install_command_copied` event. VITE_-prefixed, so it's exposed to the
# browser — that's fine, it's a public write-only ingestion key.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Server-side (registry channel): the `component_installed` event fired when
# `shadcn add` fetches /r/<variant>/<name>.json. NOT VITE_-prefixed — stays on
# the server, never shipped to the browser. Can be the same key as above.
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
